    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "- Contact Delaney Estates to arrange your viewing today E:sales@delaneyestates.ie T:018058031 -\n\nDescription\n\nDelaney Estates are delighted to present 83 Blackheath Park, Clontarf, Dublin 3, to the market. This fine three-bedroom semi-detached house with side garage and stunning long south-facing rear garden extending to circa 80 ft in length. While this wonderful home has been very well maintained by the current owners, it offers the new owner`s significant scope for further development and modernisation throughout.\n\nThe accommodation extends to a total floor area of approx. 125 sq m (with the additional benefit of the side garage, attic conversion and lean-to utility). Accommodation comprises a welcoming porch, entrance hallway with understairs storage, front living room, rear spacious dining room which overlooks the sunny rear garden, and an extended kitchen/breakfast room which leads to a side lean-to utility.\n\nOn the first floor, there is a roomy landing, three generous-sized bedrooms, a family bathroom with bath and electric shower overhead, wash hand basin and W.C., and a guest W.C. with toilet. A large attic conversion offers two additional rooms which could serve a number of uses, such as a home office, study or extra storage.\n\nBlackheath Park is situated between Vernon Avenue and Castle Avenue in a very central and sought-after location in the heart of Clontarf. Within a short stroll of a variety of shops, excellent primary and secondary schools, a great choice of restaurants, bars, coffee shops and supermarkets, with stunning coastal walks right on your doorstep. Killester DART station is within a few minutes` walk of this property, with numerous bus routes on your doorstep, and the M50 Motorway, Dublin Airport and city centre are all just a short commute away.\n\nAccommodation\n\nGround Floor\n\nPorch\n\nEntrance Hall\n\nCarpet. Understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room\nCarpet. Solid fuel fireplace\n\nDining Room\nCarpet. Glass-panelled doors.\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room\nPart carpet / part linoleum floor. Floor-to-eye-level units, plumbed for dishwasher and electric cooker.\n\nLean-to Utility Area\nPlumbed with washing machine. Provides access to the side garage and leads to the rear garden.\n\nGarage\nWired with electricity.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nLanding\nCarpet.\n\nBathroom\nBath with electric shower overhead, wash hand basin and W.C. Hot press.\nGuest W.C.\nToilet.\n\nBedroom 1\nCarpet.\n\nBedroom 2\nCarpet. Built-in wardrobes. Original tiled fireplace\n\nBedroom 3\nCarpet. Built-in storage\n\nAttic Conversion\nRoom 1: Carpet. Built-in storage in eaves.\nRoom 2: Carpet. Built-in storage in eaves.\n\nOutside\nFront: Sizeable driveway providing private off-street parking, with access to the side garage. Front garden laid in lawn.\n\nRear: A particularly attractive, long south-facing rear garden extending to circa 80 ft in length. The garden is laid mainly in lawn and enjoys excellent natural light and a sunny aspect, providing a generous private outdoor space.\n\n"
      },
